Project Mu: no Google blue on the Incognito and Guest pages

The Incognito / Guest New Tab page hard-codes Google blues for its links
and its "Learn more" button. Draw them in washi (the page's text colour)
and underline them, like the rest of Mu's UI.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_incognito_guest/incognito_and_guest_tab.css b/chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_incognito_guest/incognito_and_guest_tab.css
index a453004920..237f7f5529 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_incognito_guest/incognito_and_guest_tab.css
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_incognito_guest/incognito_and_guest_tab.css
@@ -28,8 +28,10 @@ p {
   text-align: start;
 }
 
+/* Project Mu: links in the text colour, underlined, instead of Google blue. */
 a {
-  color: rgb(51, 103, 214);
+  color: inherit;
+  text-decoration: underline;
 }
 
 a:hover {
@@ -37,7 +39,7 @@ a:hover {
 }
 
 .learn-more-button {
-  color: rgb(66, 133, 244);
+  color: inherit;
   display: inline-block;
   font-size: 92.8%;
   font-weight: 500;
@@ -47,7 +49,7 @@ a:hover {
 
 @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
   :-webkit-any(a, .learn-more-button) {
-    color: rgb(138, 180, 248);  /* --google-blue-300 */
+    color: rgb(226, 232, 240);  /* Project Mu: washi, not Google blue */
   }
 }
 
diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_incognito_guest/incognito_tab.css b/chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_incognito_guest/incognito_tab.css
index 9c5ca7a283..689bd19e61 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_incognito_guest/incognito_tab.css
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_incognito_guest/incognito_tab.css
@@ -133,7 +133,8 @@ em {
 
 .learn-more-button,
 #cookie-controls-description a {
-  color: rgb(138, 180, 248);
+  color: rgb(226, 232, 240);  /* Project Mu: washi, not Google blue */
+  text-decoration: underline;
 }
 
 /** Layout ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
